<title>JAPAN: Mazda targets 3.5-4.0 pct global car market share.</title>
<headline>Mazda targets 3.5-4.0 pct global car market share.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mazda Motor Corp President Henry Wallace said on Thursday that the company was aiming at a global market share of 3.5 to 4.0 percent in the long term.</p>
<p>He added that the carmaker had targetted a 7.0 percent share of Japan's domestic vehicle market by the turn of the century.</p>
<p>He said Mazda's global market share was now around two percent, while the domestic market share was about five percent.</p>
</text>
